  {
    "insert": "In scientific writing, one of the most important things is citing the claims and ideas to provide evidence, demonstrate engagement, give credit to the work of other researchers and make your own work more credible for readers. The proposal lacks of citations to support the claims made. For instance, there is no citations in your motivation. Without citations, the points you raise come across as opinions rather than evidence-based insights, which can weaken the academic value of your work. The proposal schould be supported with more scientific research.\n\n"
